    "roles": ["band_member", "composer", "producer"],
    "summary": "Queen's drummer from 1970, with Brian May from Smile, Freddie Mercury and John Deacon, and the band's high harmonies. A Truro schoolboy who taught himself to tune his drums after Keith Moon's records, he played one bass drum and a big Ludwig with thin heads, tuned to ring: 'I wanted to hear the drums resonate.' His parts are built for the song, 'What does the song need?': hats or the ride bell on the beat in Keep Yourself Alive, Stone Cold Crazy at 240, Bohemian Rhapsody's ballad and its rock section's kick in quarters across 12/8, Somebody to Love and We Are the Champions in 6/8, the crash ridden in Fat Bottomed Girls, Don't Stop Me Now, the loop of Another One Bites the Dust, Hammer to Fall. He wrote Radio Ga Ga and A Kind of Magic, and co-wrote Under Pressure."
  },
